{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["And blessed is El Elyon; with His might He leads, by the hand of the messenger of His vision; in the light of the sun He shines, to command him on the mountain, to prepare for Him a tent for His dwelling, as written in the pericale of VaYakhel." "<b>VaYakhel.</b> The reason of va-yakhel is that all would hear from him the matter of the Tabernacle, that they should donate. And the meaning of \"these are the words\" is the Tabernacle and its vessels to make them; therefore it is written \"to make them.\" And behold, the reason [is]: HaShem commanded me that you shall make what I say to you, and He warned you — even though the making of heaven [i.e., the Tabernacle] you are obligated to make, guard yourselves lest you do any labor on the Sabbath; and one who transgresses before witnesses, the court shall put him to death, and in another place he will explain that it is by stoning."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:31.458224408Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}